# Presentation Creation Rules

Rules for professional slide deck creation and automation.

## 1. Slide Structure and Content

- **One Idea Per Slide**: Each slide should communicate exactly one key message.
- **Bullet Limit**: Maximum 6 bullets per slide; each bullet at most 2 lines.
- **Avoid Paragraphs**: Use short phrases, not full sentences, on slides (speaker notes carry the narrative).
- **Title Convention**: Every slide must have a unique, descriptive title (not "Slide 1" or "Overview").

## 2. Visual Design

- **Template First**: Apply the slide master template before adding content to ensure consistent styling.
- **Color Discipline**: Use a maximum of 3 colors per slide from the defined palette.
- **Font Pairing**: One font for headings (bold, 28-36pt), one for body (24-28pt). No more.
- **Image Quality**: All images at 150 DPI minimum. Prefer PNG for graphics, JPEG for photographs.
- **Chart Cleanliness**: Remove default gridlines, legends placed inside chart area, direct labels where possible.
- **Consistency**: Use a single slide master throughout the deck.

## 3. Animations and Transitions

- **Purposeful**: Use animation to reveal complex information progressively, never for decoration.
- **Consistent Transition**: Use a single transition type throughout the deck (e.g., Fade or Push).
- **Timing**: Set uniform transition duration (0.5-1.0 seconds). Avoid auto-advance for content slides.
- **Restraint**: Maximum 2 animation effects per slide. No bouncing, swivel, or whimsical effects in professional decks.

## 4. Speaker Notes

- **Narrative**: Speaker notes should read as spoken narrative, not slide content rephrased.
- **Timing Cues**: Include approximate speaking time per slide in notes (e.g., "[2 min]").
- **Technical Notes**: Note transitions requiring manual intervention or presenter click-through.

## 5. Export and Delivery

- **PDF Export**: Use `ppt-master export pdf` or python-pptx for distribution to non-PowerPoint users.
- **File Size**: Compress images before embedding. Target <5MB for standard decks, <20MB for image-heavy decks.
- **Compatibility**: Save in .pptx format. Verify backward compatibility with target PowerPoint version.
- **Multiple Formats**: Generate PDF for print, PPTX for live presentation, PNG sequence for web embedding when needed.
